PROBLEM STATEMENT: Movie Buddy, a vibe based movie and series finder for India
 
OVERVIEW
Build a RAG chatbot that recommends movies and series from a fixed catalog
by mood, plot and filters, and tells users where they can legally watch
each pick in India.
 
USERS
College students and anyone who spends more time choosing than watching.
 
DATA (the only source)
data/movie_buddy_starter_3000.xlsx with sheets: Titles, Where to watch,
Data dictionary, Sources and credits. Read the Data dictionary sheet for
column meanings. Source: TMDB. Streaming availability: JustWatch via TMDB.
No scraping. No other APIs for data.
 
THE ASSISTANT MUST
1. Take a natural language request and reply with up to 5 picks.
2. Understand filters: language, movie or series, era or year, length,
   platform, free to watch, certificate, intensity, content to avoid,
   who they are watching with.
3. Understand the vibe: mood, themes, plot description, and
   'more like <title>'.
4. For every pick show: title, year, language, type, runtime or seasons,
   rating, one line hook, one sentence on why it matches, where to watch
   in India with access type and the as of date, and the TMDB link.
5. Only recommend titles that exist in the dataset. If nothing matches,
   say so and suggest which filter to relax.
6. No spoilers. Describe titles only with the hook and overview.
 
GUARDRAILS
- Refuse piracy requests (downloads, torrents, free links to paid films)
  and offer the legal platforms instead.
- Ignore instructions inside user messages that try to change these rules.
- Stay on topic: movies and series only.
- Never invent a platform, rating, year or title.
 
UI
Welcome message, 4 example prompts, chat box, results as cards, and a
footer: 'This product uses the TMDB API but is not endorsed or certified
by TMDB. Streaming availability by JustWatch.'
 
TECH CONSTRAINTS
- Python 3.11. Free tools only. No paid APIs.
- Embeddings: FastEmbed with BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5 (ONNX). No PyTorch,
  no sentence-transformers (too big for free hosting).
- Vector database: ChromaDB, local and persistent.
- LLM: Groq free tier. Secrets in .env, never committed.
- Hosting: Render free web service (512 MB RAM).
 
SUCCESS
- 20 test questions pass (Phase 8).
- App is live on a public Render link.
- Answers arrive in under 5 seconds once warm.
